    "ls|LS17_S1_U_268": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *268\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 11.07.2019\n \n \nSETTING UP OF MSME\ns\n \n \n*268  \n \n \nSHRI TIRATH SINGH RAWAT:\n \n \n \nDR. T. R. PAARIVENDHAR:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government has prepared any concrete industrial policy/action \nplan to set up Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in the hilly districts of \nUttarakhand so as \nto provide permanent employment and check migration keeping in \nview that people are continuously migrating from such places, particularly from Pauri \nGarhwal and if so, the details thereof;\n \n(b)\n \nwhether the Government has any proposal to set up more MSMEs in the\n \ncountry including industrially  backward  Perambalur region of Tamil Nadu and if so, \nthe details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and   \n \n(c)\n \nthe total number of MSMEs set up in the country including in Perambalur \nduring the last three years ?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER \nOF\n \nMICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) \nto (c)\n: \n    \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha\n \nStarred Question \nNo. *268 for answer on 11.07.2019\n \n \n(a) & (b):  The Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) \nimplements various schemes and programmes for promotion and development of \nMicro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) across the co\nuntry. These include the \nschemes/programmes such as Prime Minister’s Employment Generation Programme \n(PMEGP), Scheme of Fund for Regeneration of Traditional Industries (SFURTI), A \nScheme for Promoting Innovation, Rural Industry and Entrepreneurship (ASPIRE\n), \nCredit Guarantee Scheme, Credit Linked Capital Subsidy Scheme (CLCSS), Micro \nand Small Enterprises \n-\n \nCluster Development Programme (MSE\n-\nCDP), etc. \n \n \n \nThese programmes\n \nand schemes are aimed at creating conducive environment \nfor the MSMEs to grow across the country and promote employment generation.\n \n \n \n(c):  As per Udyog Aadhar Memorandum data, the total number of MSMEs registered \nin the Country and specifically in the Pe\nrambalur District in Tamilnadu during last \nthree years is given in the Table below:\n \n \n \nYear 2016\n-\n17\n \nYear 2017\n-\n18\n \nYear 2018\n-\n19\n \nTotal \n \nAll India\n \n2373223\n \n1517784\n \n2123472\n \n6014479\n \nPerambalur \nDistrict \n \n492\n \n528\n \n562\n \n1582\n \n \n \n********\n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_269": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 269 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24th June 2019 \n \nMerger of Educational Schemes  \n \n269. SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Ministry has decided to merge SS A (Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan), RMSA(Rashtriya \nMadhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan) and Centrally Sponsored Scheme on Teacher Education under \nthe Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan;  \n \n(b) if so, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(c) whether it would lead to losing of jobs by people working on contractual basis and \noutsourcing under SSA, particularly in Ka rnataka where more than two hundred people \nwould lose their jobs due to above merger; and  \n \n(d) if so, the steps taken/to be taken by the Government to protect them? \n \nAN S W E R \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’) \n \n(a) to (b): Yes, Sir. The Central Government has launched an Integrated Scheme for School \nEducation- Samagra Shiksha, from 2018-19 which subsumes the erstwhile centrally sponsored \nschemes of Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, Rashtr iya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan (RMSA) and \nTeacher Education Scheme (TE). It  is an overarching programme fo r the school education sector \nextending from pre-school to class XII and aims  to ensure inclusive and equitable quality \neducation at all levels  of school education. The Scheme for school education ‘Samagra \nShiksha’ envisages the ‘school’ as a continuum from primary, upper primary, secondary to \nhigher secondary levels.  It has been observed that separate schemes have created an artificial \ndivide of levels i.e., elementa ry and secondary within the “Sc hool Education Sector”. This may \nhave led to a duplication of efforts towards implementing similar interventions and achieving \nsimilar objectives. A single programme will le ad to an optimal utilization of budgetary \nallocations and effective use of human resources and institutional structures.  \n \n(c) & (d): Education is in the C oncurrent List of the Constituti on, a majority of the schools are \nunder the jurisdiction of respective States and Un ion Territories (UT). Hence, the recruitment, \nservice conditions and redeploymen t of teachers and ot her staff are primarily in the domain of \nrespective State Governments and UT Administrations. As per information received from State \n\nGovernment of Karnataka, the State Government Order has specified the posts for the office of \nthe State Project Director, District office, and Block office.  As per th e Karnataka Government \nOrder, 150 District Primary E ducation Programme (DPEP) posts and 743 outsourced posts have \nbeen continued under Samagra Shiksha.  \n**** \n ",
