    "ls|LS17_S1_U_417": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 417 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2019 \n \n \nVocational Education  \n \n \n†*417. SHRIMATI QUEEN OJA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a) the present status of the vocational education centres located in North -Eastern States \nincluding Assam; \n(b) the funds allocated to above-mentioned States during the last five years; \n(c) whether the Government is contemplating to bring a new policy for more effective \nimplementation of vocational education; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.       \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n2 \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 417 FOR REPLY ON 22.07.2019 ASKED BY SHRIMATI \nQUEEN OJA , HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT  REGARDING \nVOCATIONAL EDUCATION \n \n(a) to (b): Under Ministry of Human Resource Development’s purview, various skill oriented \ncourses are implemented by University Grants Commission (UGC) and All India Council for \nTechnical Education (AICTE) through Community Colleges, Bachelor of Vocation cour ses \n(BVoC) & Deen Dayal Upadhyaya (DDU) Kausal Kendras to boost the employability of \nyouth. All the universities and colleges in the country have the option of adopting these \napproved skill education courses . Currently, total 81 institutions (42 institutio ns offering \nB.VoC. degree programmes, 34 Community Colleges and 5 DDU Kaushal Kendras) are \nrunning vocational courses in the North-Eastern States including Assam. Rupees 158.43 crore \nhas been allocated to these institutions situated in the North -Eastern St ates for vocational \neducation during the last 5 years. The list of the B.Voc. colleges, Community Colleges and \nDDU Kaushal Kendras in the North -Eastern States with the details of allocation of funds to \nthem during last 5 years is at Annexure. \n \n(c) to (d): In addition to above, the following initiatives for vocational education have been \ntaken by the Government: \n(i) Scheme for Higher Education Youth for Apprenticeship and Skills (SHREYAS). \n(ii) Development of new and updated curricula for B.Voc. courses. \n(iii) Launch of a portal for facilitating Internships by AICTE. \n(iv) Internship made mandatory by AICTE.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n3 \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to ( d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 417 FOR REPLY ON 2 2.07.2019 ASKED BY SHRIMATI \nQUEEN OJA, HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING \nVOCATIONAL EDUCATION \n \nANNEXURE \nList of the North-Eastern Institutions offering B.Voc. Degree Programme  \n \nS. \nNo. \nName of the Institutions  Approved courses Allocation \n(Last 5 \nyears) \n (In Crore) \n Assam   \n1.  Abhayapuri College,  \nP.O. Abhayapuri, Dist. Bongaigaon-783 384, Assam. \nAffiliated to:- \nGauhati University, GopinathBardoloi Nagar, \nGuwahati - 781014, Assam \n Information Technology \n Tourism & Travel   \nManagement \n3.70 \n2.  AnandramDhekialPhookan College (A.D.P. College), \nR.R.B. Road, Haibargaon, Nagaon, Pin-782002 \n(Assam) \nAffiliated to:- \nGauhati University, GopinathBardoloi Nagar, \nGuwahati - 781014, Assam \n Herbal Processing \nTechnology \n1.45 \n3.  Biswanath College, \nChariali, PO- Chariali, Distt- Biswanath, Pin-784176 \n(Assam) \n(Affiliated to:- \nGauhati University, GopinathBardoloi Nagar, \nGuwahati - 781014, Assam \n Agriculture (Small Tea \nGarden Management) \n1.45 \n4.  Chaiduar College, Assam  \nAffiliated to:- \nGauhati University, Gopinath,  Bardoloi Nagar, \nGuwahati - 781014, Assam \n Medical Laboratory \nTechnology \n Media and Entertainment \n3.55 \n5.  DakshinKamrup College, Mirza, Kamrup Di