    "ls|LS17_S1_U_429": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED  QUESTION No. *429 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 23RD JULY, 2019  \n \n \n \nInfrastructure of Fishing Ports \n \n*429. SHRI SELVAM G:  \n          \n \nWill the Minist er of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nमत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n \n \n(a)  the details of the action taken so far by the Government to improve the infrastructure \nof various fishing ports in Tamil Nadu;  \n \n(b)  whether the Government has carried out any survey to iden tify fishing ports which \nlack infrastructure and other facilities, especially in Tamil Nadu and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  whether the Government has received any proposal from various States for survey of \nfishing ports in certain coastal States; and  \n \n(d)  if so, the details of proposals submitted for establishment of new fishing ports during \nthe last three years and the current year, State/UT-wise? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n (SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n(a) to  (d)  :        A Statement is placed on the Table of the House. \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No.429 put in by Shri \nSelvam G, Member of Parliament for answer on 23rd July, 2019  regarding \nInfrastructure of Fishing Ports  \n \n \n \n(a) to (d) :   Department of Fisheries (DoF), Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and \nDairying under the Centrally Sponsored Scheme(CSS) on Blue Revolution: Integrated \nDevelopment and Management of Fisheries  provides financial assistance to the State \nGovernments/State Agencies, Union Territories and Central Government \nAgencies/Organizations for development of new fishing harbours, fish landing centres and \nUp-gradation/expansion/ repair/renovation of the existing ones. The CSS on Blue Revolution: \nIntegrated Development and Management of Fisheries  provides funds for development of \nfishing ports to the State Governments /State Agencies , Union Territories and Central \nGovernment Agencies/ Organizations, including Tamil Nadu and dovetails fund s available \nunder the Sagarmala Scheme of Ministry of Shipping. During the past three years and current \nfinancial year , central financial assistance of Rs. 203.67 crore has been provided to the \nGovernment of Tamil Nadu for construction of fishing harbours facilities at Thengapattinam, \nPoompuhar, Colachel, Mookaiyur, expansion of Chinnamuttam Fishing Harbour and one fish \nlanding centre at Kunthukal. Besides, the Government of Tamil Nadu has reported \nconstruction of one new fishing harbour at Mallipattinam, modernization of two fishing \nharbours at Napattinam and Pazhyar with a total cost of Rs137.43 crore with the assistance of \nWorld Bank under Coastal Disaster Risk Reduction Project. The Government of Tamil Nadu \nfurther reported that the Chennai Fishing Harbour has been upgrade d, modernized and \nrenovated at total cost of Rs. 97.63 crore with financial assistance from various agencies such \nas NABARD, National Fisheries Development Board(NFDB) and Tsunami Rehabilitation \nProgramme and NADP.   \n \nFormulation of proposals, construction , post-construction management of the  fishing \nharbours are done by the concerned State Governments /Union Territories(UTs) and in some \ncases by the Port Trusts.  To seek the central financial assistance under the CSS on Blue \nRevolution: Integrated Develop ment and Management of Fisheries , the concerned State \nGovernments/UTs/ Port Trusts are to complete pre -implementation activities , such  as \nselection of site,  completion of necessary engineering and  socio-economic investigations , \nsurveys, hydraulic model stu dies wherever  required, land  acquisition if required, obtain  \nenvironmental clearance etc and to submit the Detailed Project Report (DPR). Further, at the \nrequest of the State Governments/UTs/Port T rusts, t he Ministry of Fisheries, Animal \n\nHusbandry and D airying throug h one of its institutes namely Central Institute of Coastal \nEngineering for F ishery(CICEF), Bengaluru also assists the State G overnments/UTs/Port \nTrusts in conducting necessary surveys to carry out reconnaissance surveys followed by \ndetailed eng ineering & economic investigations and formulation of techno -economic \nfeasibility reports and primarily construction plans for fishery harbour and fish landing \ncentres, besides gives technical advice on eng ineering and economic aspects. D uring the past \nthree years, CICEF, Bengaluru, based o n the request of the concerned S tate/UT, conducted \nsurveys at (i) two fishing harbours in Puducherry namely Thengaithittu and Karaikal to assess \nthe infrastructure gaps and deman ds, (ii) phase -ii expansion of Astranga F ishing harbour in \nOdisha, (iii) Gopalpur Fishing Harbour in Odisha and (iv) Sassoon dock in Maharashtra.  \nDetails of the proposals submitted by the States/UTs for setting up new fishing \nharbours as well as expansion/modernisation of the existing ones during the past three years \n(2016-17 to 2018-19) and current year (2019-20) under the CSS are furnished at Annexure -I.   \nDetails of the fishing harbour proposals submitted under Fisheries and Aquaculture \nInfrastructure Development Fund (FIDF) are furnished at Annexure-II. \n***** \n\nAnnexure-I \nAnnexure referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 429 for answer on \n23rd July, 2019 regarding Infrastructure of Fishing Ports –  \n \nDetails of the proposals submitted by the State/UTs for setting up of new fishing \nharbours including expansion/up-gradation of existing ones \n \n \nSl \nNo \nName of \nthe \nState/UT \nName of the fishing harbour  District Estimated cost \n(Rs. in lakhs)   \n1. Expansion/up-gradation of existing Fishing Harbours \n1.1 Maharashtra  Sassoon Dock Mumbai 5217.00 \n1.2 Gujarat  3rd Stage of Mangrol Fishing Harbour Junagadh 15583.00 \n1.3 Puducherry  Up-gradation of Thengaithittu Fishing \nHarbour \nPuducherry 1563.00 \nPhase-II Expansion of Yanam Fishing \nHarbour \nYanam 3358.00 \n2. New Fishing Harbours \n2.1 Tamil Nadu Mookaiyur  Ramanathapuram 11390.00 \n2.2 Karnataka \n \nKulai Dakshina \nKannada \n19651.00 \nHejamadi kodi Udupi 13860.00 \n2.3 Maharashtra Karanja Raigad 14980.00 \nAnandwadi Shindhudurg 8844.00 \nVersova  Mumbai  \nSuburban  \n33670.00 \n2.4 Orissa Chandipur Balasore 4994.00 \n2.5 Gujarat Navabandar  Junagadh 29530.00 \nMadhavad Junagadh 11576.00 \n2.6 Andhra \nPradesh  \nJuvvaladinne SPSR Nellore 28856.00 \n***** \n\nAnnexure-II \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No.429  for answer on \n23rd July, 2019 regarding Infrastructure of Fishing Ports –  \n \nDetails of the proposals submitted by the State Government s for setting up of new \nfishing harbours including expansion/up-gradation of existing ones for financing under \nthe Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund (FIDF). \n \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n  \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the Fishing Harbour  District  Estimated cost \n(Rs. In lakhs) \nA Proposal of the Government of Tamil Nadu  \n1. Tharangampadi  Nagapattinam 12000.00 \n2. Vellapallam  Nagapattinam 10000.00 \n3. Thiruvottriyur Kuppam  Tiruvallur 20000.00 \n4. Development of existing Fishing Harbour at \nMudhunagar, Cuddalore  \nCuddalore 10000.00 \n Total  52000.00 \nB Proposal of the Government of Andhra Pradesh \n1 Uppada East Godavari 28940.00 \n2 Vodarevu Prkasham 40922.00 \n3 Machilipattinam Krishna 25200.00 \n4 Nizampattinam Guntur 34078.00 \n Total  129140.00 \n Grant total(A+B)  192740.00 ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_431": " \nO.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE,\n \nCOOPERATION\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n431\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE\n, 2019\n \n \nUPLIFTMENT OF FARMERS\n \n \n \n431. \n    \nSHRIMATI RANJAN BEN DHANANJAY BHATT: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n\t\n\u0000कसान\n\t\nक\u0000याण\n\t\nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government proposes to formulate any special scheme for the \nupliftment of the farmers;\n \n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif\n \nso, whether the Government has taken any step in this direction yet; and \n \n \n(c)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n   \n(\nSHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR\n)\n \n \n(a) & (b):\n \nAgriculture is a State subject.  Government of India facilitates the State \nGovernments through Centrally Sponsored Schemes and Central Sector Schemes, \nwhich are for the upliftment of farmers.  A list of schemes administered by the \nDepartment o\nf Agriculture Cooperation, Farmers’ Welfare is annexed at \nAnnexure\n-\nI.\n \n \n(c):\n \nThe financial allocation for all Centrally Sponsored and Central Sector Schemes \nduring the last 3 years is as under:\n-\n \n \n(Rs. In Crore)\n \nCategory\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \nBudget \nEstimate\n \n35983.69\n \n41105.00\n \n46700.00\n \nRevised Estimate\n \n39840.50\n \n41855.00\n \n67800.00\n \nActual Release\n \n37029.82\n \n37538.77\n \n46583.50\n \n*Actuals is provisional for 2018\n-\n19\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nANNEXURE\n-\nI\n \n \nANNEXURE TO LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 431 DUE ON 25.\n06.2019.\n \n \n \nSl.\n \nNo\n \nName of the Scheme\n \n1\n.\n \n \nInterest Subsidy for Short Term Credit to \nFarmers \n \n2\n.\n \n \nPradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojna \n-\nNCIP \n \n3\n.\n \n \nPradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojna\n-\nPer \nDrop More Crop \n \n4\n.\n \n \nImplementation of Market Intervention Scheme/Price Support Scheme \n \n5\n.\n \n \nPromotion \nof Agricultural Mechanization for in\n-\nsitu Management of Crops \nResidue\n \n6\n.\n \n \nPradhan Mantri Annadata Aay Sanrakshan \nAbhiyan\n \n(PM\n-\nAASHA)\n \n7\n.\n \n \nDistribution of Pulses for Welfare Schemes\n \n8\n.\n \n \nPM\n-\nKISAN (INCOME Support Scheme)\n \n9\n.\n \n \nPM\n-\nKISAN \n-\n \nPension\n \n10\n.\n \n \nNational Beekeeping \nHoney Mission (NBHM)\n \n \nGREEN REVOLUTION\n \n11\n.\n \n \nRastriya Krishi Vikas \nYojna \n \n \nKRISHONNATI  YOJANA\n \n12\n.\n \n \nIntegrated Development of \nHorticulture \n \n \nNational Mission for Sustainable Agriculture\n \n13\n.\n \n \nNational Project on promotion of Organic \nFarming \n \n14\n.\n \n \nNational Project on Management of Soil \nHealth & Fertility \n \n15\n.\n \n \nOrganic Value Chain Development for NES \nRegion\n \n16\n.\n \n \nMission for Sustainable Agriculture (RADP)\n \n17\n.\n \n \nSoil and Land Use Survey of India\n \n18\n.\n \n \nParamparagat Krishi Vikas Yojna\n \n19\n.\n \n \nNational Project on \nAgro\n-\nForestry\n \n20\n.\n \n \nNational \nBamboo\n \nMission\n \n \nNational Mission on Agricultural Extension & Technology\n \n21\n.\n \n \nSub\n-\nMission on Agriculture Extension\n \n22\n.\n \n \nInformation Technology\n \n23\n.\n \n \nSub\n-\nMission Seeds & Planting Material\n \n24\n.\n \n \nSub\n-\nMission on Agricultural Mechanization\n \n25\n.\n \n \nStrengthening/Promoting Agricultural Information Systems\n \n26\n.\n \n \nSub\n-\nMission on Plant Protection and Plant \nQuarantine\n \n27\n.\n \n \nIntegrated Scheme on Agriculture \nCooperation\n \n28\n.\n \n \nIntegrated scheme on Agricultural \nMarke\nting\n \n \nNational Food Security Mission\n \n29\n.\n \n \nNational Food \nSecurity Mission  \n-\n \nOilseeds and Oil Palm\n \n30\n.\n \n \nNational Food Security Mission    \n-\n  \nOther Crops\n \n31\n.\n \n \nIntegrated Scheme on Agriculture Census and Statistics\n \n32\n.\n \n \nNational Rainfed Area Authority\n \n \n******\n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_432": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 432 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.06.2019 \n \nSTEPS TO PROMOTE ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRY AND FISHERY SECTORS \n \n 432. SHRI SHIVAKUMAR C. UDASI: \n \n Will the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  मात्स्यिकी, पशुपालन और डेिरी मंत्री  \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to give more importance to Animal Husbandry, Dairy and \nFishery sectors and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(b) whether it has become necessary to pay more attention towards milch cattle due to irregular \nrain and shortage of water in various parts of the country and if so, the steps proposed to be taken \nby the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n (a)  Yes, Sir.  The Government is implementing various schemes to supplement the efforts of \nStates/UTs for development of animal husbandry and fisheries sectors namely, \n  \nI. Rashtriya Gokul Mission  \nII. National Programme for Dairy Development  \nIII. National Dairy Plan-I \nIV. Dairy Entrepreneurship Development Scheme \nV. Dairy Processing and Infrastructure Development Fund \nVI. Supporting Dairy Cooperatives and Farmer Producer Organizations engaged in dairy \nactivities \nVII. National Livestock Mission \nVIII. Livestock Health & Disease Control \nIX. Blue Revolution: Integrated Development and Management of Fisheries \nX. Fisheries and Aquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund \n  \nIn addition, recently, the Cabinet in its 1 st meeting held on 31.05.2019 has approved an \nambitious scheme “ National Animal Disease Control Programme (NADCP) for control of Foot & \nMouth Disease and Brucellosis” by vaccinating 100% cattle, buffalo, sheep, goat and pig population \nfor FMD and 100% bovine female calves of 4 -8 months of age for brucellosis. The programme has \na total outlay of Rs.13,343.00 crore for five years (2019-20 to 2023-24). \n(b) Yes, Sir. The Government issues advisory to the States/UTs to mitigate drought or drought like \nsituation due to deficit rainfall. The Government has also developed Disaster management plan in \nconsultation with National Disaster Management Authority. \n****** ",
