    "ls|LS17_S1_U_438": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED  QUESTION No. *438 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 23RD JULY, 2019  \n \n \n \nMarine and Aquaculture Products \n \n*438. SHRI BALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI:  \n          \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nमत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n \n \n(a) the details of the production and export of marine and aquaculture products in the \ncountry during the last five years and the current year, year and State-wise; \n \n(b) whether it is true that the Govern ment has approved Fisheries and Aquaculture \nInfrastructure Development Fund (FAIDF); \n  \n(c) if so, the aims and objectives of the Fund; \n \n(d) the extent to which the Fund has helped/will help in creating critical infrastructure, \ntechnology infusion, marketing, etc. in major marine and aquaculture producing States like \nAndhra Pradesh; and  \n \n(e) the estimated number of employment opportunities which would be created through \nutilisation of this Fund, State-wise along with the extent to which FAIDF would help in Blue \nRevolution? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n (SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n(a) to  (e)  :        A Statement is placed on the Table of the House. \n \n*****\n\nStatement referred to in reply to the Lok Sabha Starred Question No.*438 put in by \nShri Balashowry Vallabhaneni, Member of Parliament for answer on 23rd July, 2019 \nregarding Marine and Aquaculture Products \n \n (a) : State-wise details of the fish production and export of marine and aquaculture products \nin the country  during the last five years are furnished at Annexure-I and Annexure-II \nrespectively. \n \n \n \n(b) to (e) : Yes, Sir.  In order to address the infrastructure requirement for fisheries sector, the \nGovernment of India during 2018 -19 a created dedicated fund  namely Fisheries and \nAquaculture Infrastructure Development Fund (FIDF ) with a total funds size of Rs 7522.48 \ncrore with the objectives  of  creation and modernization of inland and marine fisheries  \ninfrastructure, infrastructure support for improving domestic marketing facilities  and to \nbridge the resource gap and facilitate completion of ongoing infrastructure projects.  \nThe FIDF provides concessional finance to the Eligible Entities (EEs), including State \nGovernments/Union Territories and State entities for development of identified  fisheries \ninfrastructure facilities. The concessional finance is provided by the Nodal Loaning Entities \n(NLEs) namely (i) National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development (NABARD),  (ii) \nNational Cooperatives Development Corporation (NCDC)  and (iii) All scheduled Banks .  \nUnder the FIDF, the Government of India provides interest subvention up to 3% per annum  \nfor providing concessional finance by the NLEs at an  interest rate n ot lower than 5% per \nannum.  \nThe infrastructure facilities envisaged under FIDF for the benefit  of fisheries sector  in \nall the States/Union Territories including Andhra Pradesh are :  establishment of fishing \nharbours and fish landing centres,  ice plants, cold storages,  fish transport and cold chain \nnetwork infrastructure, m odern fish markets, s etting up of brood banks and h atcheries, \ndevelopment of aquaculture and mariculture,  modernization of state fish seed farms,  state of \nart fisheries training centres, f ish processing units, f ish feed mills/plants, e stablishment of \ncage culture in reservoirs, introduction of deep sea fishing vessels, establishment of disease \ndiagnostic laboratories, and a quatic quarantine facilities etc. FIDF aims to achieve a \nsustainable growth of 8 -9 per cent, in a move to augment the country’s fish production and \ngenerate both direct and indirect employment opportunities to over 9 lakh persons in fishing \nand allied activities.  \n*****\n\n \n \nAnnexure-I \n \nStatement referred  to in reply to the parts ( a) of the Lok Sabha starred Question No. \n438 for answer on 2 3rd July 2019 regarding Marine and Aquaculture Products : State–\nwise details of the fish production during the last five years. \n \n(Quantity in  000’tonnes) \nS.N. State/Uts 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17  2017-18 (P) 2018-19 (E) \nTotal Total Total Total Total \n1 Andhra Pradesh 1978.58 2352.26 2766.19 3449.56 3992.36 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 4.00 4.05 4.11 4.25 4.67 \n3 Assam 282.70 294.20 306.60 327.26 331.53 \n4 Bihar 479.80 506.89 509.08 587.85 602.13 \n5 Chhattisgarh 314.16 342.30 376.80 457.17 469.76 \n6 Goa 117.98 111.91 117.89 124.01 120.29 \n7 Gujarat 809.93 809.56 815.56 834.53 724.67 \n8 Haryana 111.20 121.00 144.21 190.00 217.53 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 10.74 11.80 12.51 12.77 13.40 \n10 J & K 20.30 20.08 20.39 20.70 22.44 \n11 Jharkhand 106.43 116.00 145.16 190.00 208.00 \n12 Karnataka 623.24 580.57 557.49 602.52 587.41 \n13 Kerala 726.01 727.51 592.85 562.62 714.46 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 109.12 115.02 138.69 143.42 173.19 \n15 Maharashtra 608.07 579.69 662.91 606.01 583.38 \n16 Manipur 30.50 32.04 32.00 33.00 32.15 \n17 Meghalaya  6.04 11.34 12.33 11.96 0.01 \n18 Mizoram 6.39 6.83 7.63 7.64 7.23 \n19 Nagaland 7.84 8.22 8.61 8.99 9.78 \n20 Odisha 469.55 521.28 608.10 684.96 733.43 \n21 Punjab 114.77 120.09 132.72 136.64 135.83 \n22 Rajasthan 45.42 42.46 50.20 54.04 55.85 \n23 Sikkim 0.44 0.40 0.38 0.38 0.39 \n24 Tamil Nadu 697.61 709.16 669.31 712.04 730.67 \n25 Telangana 268.36 236.75 198.92 270.04 328.41 \n26 Tripura 65.16 69.06 72.45 76.80 84.53 \n27 Uttarakhand 3.94 4.14 4.30 4.58 4.95 \n28 Uttar Pradesh 494.27 504.81 617.69 628.75 662.00 \n29 West Bengal 1617.32 1671.42 1701.82 1742.09 1770.31 \n30 A&N Islands 37.18 37.33 38.81 39.50 41.19 \n31 Chandigarh             0.12 0.13 0.13 0.14 0.16 \n32 Dadra & N Haveli 0.06 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 \n33 Daman & Diu 31.82 23.03 24.02 24.68 5.38 \n34 Delhi 0.68 0.71 0.95 0.80 0.79 \n35 Lakshadweep 13.19 15.94 29.80 20.77 21.91 \n36 Puducherry 47.40 53.81 50.25 49.92 31.38 \n Total 10260.28 10761.76 11430.84 12620.39 13421.56 \nNote; P: Provisional, E: Estimated \n \n*****\n\n \nAnnexure-II \nStatement referred  to in reply to the par ts (a) of the  Lok Sabha starred Question No. \n438 for answer on 2 3rd July 2019 regarding Marine and Aquaculture Products  – State-\nwise details of the export of marine and aquaculture fish products during the last five \nyears. \n \n \nQ: Quantity in Tonnes, V: Value in Rs. Crore, $: US Dollar in  Million \nSTATE   2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19* \nGUJARAT Q: 251920 245434 208624 237442 312568 305113 \n  V: 3658.56 3645.23 3567.24 4417.40 5071.05 5199.93 \n  $: 604.51 597.84 546.31 659.70 791.38 744.28 \nMAHARASHTRA Q: 147411 151684 127629 151753 180820 155288 \n  V: 3986.11 4273.29 3672.99 4311.65 4906.82 5964.78 \n  $: 661.23 703.33 565.25 650.12 772.68 874.04 \nGOA Q: 34288 44684 31681 43199 50571 36501 \n  V: 445.92 569.54 490.48 641.41 711.91 606.16 \n  $: 72.13 93.38 75.09 96.79 111.73 86.32 \nKARNATAKA Q: 98619 116323 84032 126607 144296 141799 \n  V: 1122.39 1374.97 1050.38 1589.05 1796.68 1887.53 \n  $: 184.09 225.11 160.99 279.20 282.05 269.43 \nKERALA Q: 165698 166754 149138 159141 178646 167130 \n  V: 4706.36 5166.08 4644.42 5008.54 5919.03 5180.70 \n  $: 784.79 851.27 714.60 755.46 929.62 748.57 \nTAMIL NADU Q: 94843 93477 85063 88257 114370 120742 \n  V: 4874.28 5038.18 4184.06 4341.78 5408.82 5546.75 \n  $: 815.60 830.64 646.49 654.71 850.09 805.24 \nANDRA \nPRADESH  Q: 121975 147081 168323 223636 290521 305319 \n  V: 8360.49 9671.32 9369.76 13066.17 16381.37 16372.38 \n  $: 1381.17 1597.79 1446.67 1970.36 2572.75 2372.32 \nWEST BENGAL Q: 68752 85551 91397 104786 105318 107453 \n  V: 3058.67 3696.67 3441.17 4459.26 4909.71 4799.10 \n  $: 504.11 610.74 532.50 705.96 771.02 694.65 \nAs  there is no ports in Odisha handling reefer cargo, the export from the State of Odisha is happening through \nthe ports of West Bengal and Andhra Pradesh.       \n         \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_439": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 439 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 25TH JUNE, 2019/ ASHADHA 4, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nOBJECTIONABLE PHOTOS ON FACEBOOK \n \n†439. SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware   that in the year 2018, the photos \nand mobile  numbers of many women were uploaded  on facebook to \ndefame them as call girls  and the police has not taken any action  \nagainst the culprits even after the  registration of the complaint in the \nCrime Branch; \n \n(b) if so, the number of such  complaints registered in the Crime Branch  \nsituated at Mandir Marg and Dwarka in  which no action has been taken \nagainst the culprits; and \n \n(c) the reasons for inactivity of the police in this regard along with the \nstatus of the said cases as on date? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n(a), (b) & (c): Delhi Police registers all cognizable complaints with an \nobjective that no crime , especially crime against the vulnerable group s \nincluding women and girls, goes unreported and action in all such cases \nis taken as per provisions of Law. In the year 2018, 18 such cases were \nregistered in which photos and mobile numbers of women were \nuploaded to defame them. In 2019 (up to 31.05.2019) , 2 such cases \nwere registered. Appropriate legal  action has been taken in all such \ncases. 13 persons have been arrested in these cases. \n                   ********* ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_440": "O.I.H \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES,  ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 440 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.06.2019 \n \nFUNDING FOR ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \n440. SHRI DEEPAK BAIJ:  \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING मात्स्यिकी, पशुपालन और डेिरी मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n(a) the funds sanctioned for animal husbandry, dairying and fisheries during the last five years, the details \nthereof, State-wise and year-wise;  \n(b) the details of expenditure of the allotted fund; and  \n(c) the reasons for non -utilization of the allotted fund an d whether any study has been conducted in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a) to (c) The funds sanctioned, the details of expenditure of the allotted fund and non-utilised fund for \nanimal husbandry, dairying and fisheries during  the last five years, State -wise and year-wise are given at \nAnnexure-I to VIII.  \n \n*** \n \n \n\nAnnexure-I \nState-wise and year-wise funds released, utilized and unspent under Rashtriya Gokul Mission during the last five years \n(Rs. In lakhs) \nSN Name of \nthe \nState/Uts \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 Total \nReleased Utilized Released Utilized Released Utilized Released Utilized Released Utilized Released Utilized Unspen\nt Bal \n1 Andhra \nPradesh \n600.00 600.00 0.00 0.00 675.00 675.00 437.45 437.45 1899.81 1513.64 3612.26 3226.09 386.17 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh \n0.00 0.00 264.50 264.50 14.81 14.81 200.00 200.00 14.75 10.47 494.06 489.78 4.28 \n3 Assam 200.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 287.15 0.00 0.00 0.00 4896.10 50.00 5383.25 50.00 5333.2\n5 \n4 Bihar 0.00 0.00 750.00 750.00 0.00 0.00 5989.95 4196.79 6202.83 3202.83 12942.78 8149.62 4793.16 \n5 Chattisgarh 1080.00 1046.51 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00 100.00 100.00 2640.42 18.29 3820.42