    "ls|LS17_S1_U_467": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.467 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.07.2019 \n \nERRATIC POWER SUPPLY BY POWER DISTRIBUTION COMPANIES \n \n†*467. SHRI JANARDAN MISHRA: \n SHRI RODMAL NAGAR: \n \nWill the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has formulated  any scheme to avoid \nerratic power  supply by the power distribution companies  even after \ncarrying out the maintenance before the rainy season; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  if not, the measures being taken by the Government to avoid such \nerratic power supply; and \n \n(d)  the details of action taken by the Government  against such \ncompanies for irregular supply of power? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR POWER, NEW & \nRENEWABLE ENERGY AND MINISTER OF STATE FOR SKILL \nDEVELOPMENT & ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n( SHRI  R.K. SINGH)  \n \n \n(a) to (d) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n*********** \n  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 467 TO BE ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON 25.07.2019 \nREGARDING ERRATIC POWER SUPPLY BY POWER DISTRIBUTION \nCOMPANIES. \n********* \n \n(a) to (d) :   The distribution of electricity, including maintenance of \ninfrastructure falls under the  purview of the respective State \nGovernments/ Distribution utilities, and the State Electricity Regulatory \nCommissions (SERCs).  \nThe Government of India, as per Section 57(1) and 57(2) of the \nElectricity Act 2003, has empowered the SERCs to specify the Sta ndards \nof performance (SoP) of a licensee or a class of licensees, with provisions \nfor suitable compensation in case of non -adherence. Further, as per \nSection 86 (1) (i), SERCs shall specify or enforce Standards with respect \nto the quality, continuity and reliability of service by Licensees. The \nCentral Electricity Authority (Measures relating to safety and Electric \nSupply) Regulations 2010 also provides measures for empowering \ntechnicians with training on pre -monsoon maintenance of transmission \nand distribution lines. \nFurther, the Government of India has been assisting States \nthrough various schemes including Deendayal Upadhyaya Gram Jyoti \nYojana (DDUGJY) and Integrated Power Development Scheme (IPDS) for \nstrengthening the sub -transmission and distributi on networks, metering, \nIT enablement, segregation of feeders etc. to enable 24X7 reliable power \nsupply for all. \n \n*********** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S1_U_468": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *468\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.07.2019\n \n \nACHIEVEMENTS OF KVIC\n \n \n*468.\n \n \nSHRI RAJA AMARESHWARA NAIK: \n \n \nSHRI VINOD KUMAR SONKAR: \n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC) has been \nsuccessful in achieving their objectives during the last five years and if so, the details \nthereof; \n \n(b)\n \nthe details of the development schemes/programmes being implemented by \nKVIC and the funds allocated therefor during each of the last five years, State/ UT\n-\nwise; \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has initiated any reform and development programme \nfor KVIC; \n \n(d)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof along with the extent to which it is likely to help \nKVIC in achieving its objectives and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) \n \nthe other steps being taken by the Government in this regard?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND\n \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) to (e):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY \nPARTS (a) TO (e) OF\n \nTHE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *468 FOR ANSWER ON 25.07.2019\n \n \n \n(a):\n \nYes, Sir. Khadi & Villa\nge Industries Commission (KVIC) has the objective of \ndevelopment of Khadi and Village Industries. KVIC’s endeavour towards achieving \nits objective is reflected in the table below giving figures of production, sales and \nemployment for the last five years:\n-\n \n \nYear\n \nProduction\n \n(Rs. in crore)\n \nSales\n \n(Rs.\n \nin crore)\n \nCumulative \nEmployment\n \n(No. of persons\n \nin lakhs)\n \nKhadi\n \nV.I.\n \nKhadi\n \nV.I.\n \nKhadi\n \nV.I.\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \n879.98\n \n26689.39\n \n1170.38\n \n31965.52\n \n11.06\n \n123.19\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n1065.60\n \n33424.62\n \n1510.00\n \n40384.56\n \n11.07\n \n126.76\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n1520.83\n \n41110.26\n \n2146.60\n \n49991.61\n \n4.56\n@\n \n131.84\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n1626.66\n \n46454.75\n \n2510.21\n \n56672.22\n \n4.65\n \n135.71\n \n2018\n-\n19 (P)\n \n1963.30\n \n56255.18\n \n3215.13\n \n71113.68\n \n4.95\n \n142.03\n \nNote\n: Khadi includes Polyvastra & Solarvastra from 2015\n-\n16 onwards\n \n \n \n@\n-\nAadhaarenabled\n \nfrom 2016\n-\n17onwards\n \n \nP\n-\nProvisional\n \n \n(b):\n \nKVIC is implementing a number of Central Sector Schemes of the Ministry of \nMicro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) for Khadi and Village Industries \nsector. The funds under these schemes including Prime Minister\n’\ns\n \nEmployment \nGeneration Programme (PMEGP) are given to KVIC in lump\n-\nsum and are not \nallocated State/UT wise. The important schemes are (i) Market Promotion \nDevelopment Assistance (MPDA), (ii) Interest Subsidy Eligibility Certificate (ISEC) \nand (iii) Worksh\ned Scheme for Khadi artisans.\n \n \n \n \n \n(Rs. in crore)\n \nScheme\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \nPMEGP\n \n1093.06\n \n1286.20\n \n1082.90\n \n1170.00\n \n1968.80\n \nMDA/MPDA, ISEC & \n‘Workshed Scheme for \nKhadi Artisans’\n \n250.25\n \n195.77\n \n400.41\n \n379.22\n \n197.51\n \nTotal\n \n1343.31\n \n1481.97\n \n1483.31\n \n1549.22\n \n2166.31\n \nNote\n: Market Development Assistance\n \n(\nMDA) scheme has been changed to MPDA \nfrom FY 2016\n-\n17.\n \n \nIn addition to the above\n-\nmentioned schemes, KVIC, as a nodal agency, is \nimplementing, a credit linked subsidy programme\n \nnamely, Prime Minister’s \nEmployment Generation Programme (PMEGP) for generating employment by setting \nup micro enterprises including agro rural industries in the non\n-\nfarm sector. The State\n-\nwise release of margin money subsidy, which is treated as target, \nand the \nachievements in terms of margin money subsidy utilized for setting up micro \nenterprises, for the last five years under PMEGP, is given at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n: 2 :\n \n \n \n(c) to (e):\n \nYes, Sir. The Khadi\n \nReform Development Program (KRDP) has been \ninitiated with financial assistance from Asian Development Bank (ADB). KRDP has \nbeen designed to revitalize the Khadi sector with enhanced sustainability of Khadi, \nincreased incomes and employment for spinners an\nd weavers, increased artisans’ \nwelfare and achieve synergy with village industries. ‘Khadi Reform Package’ \nenvisages reform support in the following areas: (i) Artisan Earnings and \nEmpowerment, (ii) Direct Reform Assistance to 400 Khadi Institutions & (iii\n) \nImplementation of a well\n-\nknit MIS.\n \n \n300 Khadi Institutions have been identified for reform assistance. The \nProgramme contains a provision for updation of Central Sliver Plants of KVIC, \nmarket development activities like market survey, design inputs, bran\nd building, \n‘Khadi Mark’ promotion, development of clusters in five traditional village industries, \nopening of new sales outlets in metropolitan cities and State capitals, and renovation \nand modernization of institutional sales outlets. \n \n \nKRDP is closely m\nonitored and reviewed at the level of implementing agency \ni.e KVIC and the Ministry. Efforts for systemic improvement in the light of \nimplementation problems are a continuous process. ‘Khadi Mark’ has also been \nintroduced under KRDP to guarantee the genuin\neness and purity of Khadi sold in the \nmarket. Improvement in sale of KVI products is expected by introduction of ‘Khadi \nMark’. \n \n \nNew initiatives taken by the Government for promotion of Khadi products are \nmentioned in \nAnnexure\n-\nII\n.\n \n \n* * *\n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnne\nxure\n-\nI referred to in reply to part (b) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *468 \nfor answer on 25.07.2019\n \n \nYear\n-\nwise and State\n-\nwise det